# DRAIS Mobile — what does and does not travel.
#
# ## Credentials are excluded
#
# This repository is public, so no live credential may enter it. Note that
# git history is permanent: removing a secret in a later commit does not
# unpublish it, which is why these patterns are here from the very first
# commit rather than added afterwards.
#
# Templates are committed instead — `drais.env.example` and
# `server/.env.example` — so a clone knows exactly what to fill in. See the
# README for the two-file setup, and docs/DEPLOYMENT_MODES.md for how the app
# resolves them.
#
# Everything else below is excluded because it is regenerated by a build, is
# machine-specific, or is large enough to make cloning slow.

# ── Live credentials — never commit ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `.env.example` files are exempt: they carry keys with empty values, and they
# are what makes a fresh clone runnable.
drais.env
**/drais.env
assets/drais.env
.env
**/.env
!*.env.example
!**/.env.example

# ── Build output — regenerated by `flutter build`, hundreds of MB ────────────
/build/
/coverage/
server/build/
android/.gradle/
android/app/debug/
android/app/profile/
android/app/release/
android/local.properties
**/.cxx/

# ── Generated package metadata — restored by `flutter pub get` ───────────────
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/
**/doc/api/

# NOTE: pubspec.lock IS committed, deliberately. It pins the exact dependency
# versions this app was built and tested against, which is most of what makes
# "clone it and run" reproduce the same app rather than a similar one.

# ── Platform ephemera — regenerated by the Flutter tool on first build ───────
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
ios/Flutter/ephemeral/
ios/Flutter/Generated.xcconfig
ios/Flutter/flutter_export_environment.sh
ios/Pods/
ios/.symlinks/
macos/Flutter/ephemeral/
macos/Pods/
macos/.symlinks/
linux/flutter/ephemeral/
windows/flutter/ephemeral/
**/generated_plugin_registrant.*

# ── Editor and OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.log
.history
.atom/
.svn/
.swiftpm/
migrate_working_dir/

# ── Symbolication and obfuscation artefacts ─────────────────────────────────
app.*.symbols
app.*.map.json

# ── Signing material ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Keystores are excluded even though env files are not. An env credential can
# be rotated in an afternoon; a leaked upload key cannot be replaced at all
# once an app is published under it, and Google will not reissue one.
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties
